{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T16:52:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-30T22:22:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-30T22:22:51+05:30\nThe search for \"\"GTA\" \"Spider-Man\" \"Menyoo\" \"YouTube\" monetization site:reddit.com\" returned the following summary:\nThe intersection of using mods (like **Menyoo** for **GTA**), third-party intellectual property (like **Spider-Man**), and **YouTube monetization** is a complex topic often discussed in gaming communities on Reddit[1][2].\n\n### **Key Considerations Regarding Monetization**\n\n*   **The Nature of Copyright and IP:** Using a Spider-Man character model in *Grand Theft Auto* involves two distinct layers of intellectual property: Rockstar Games (GTA) and Marvel/Sony (Spider-Man)[2]. While gameplay footage is often tolerated by developers as \"free promotion,\" using prominent third-party IP (like Spider-Man) can increase the risk of copyright strikes because it involves assets that the game publisher does not own[3][2].\n*   **\"Fair Use\" vs. Legal Reality:** Many creators argue that transformative content (e.g., adding commentary, edits, or roleplay) falls under fair use[4][2]. However, Reddit discussions frequently highlight that **fair use is a legal defense, not a guarantee**[2]. Copyright holders (especially those protecting major brands like Marvel) have the right to issue takedowns regardless of whether the video is monetized[5][2].\n*   **Publisher Stance:**\n    *   **Rockstar Games:** Historically, Rockstar has had a mixed relationship with mods[6]. While they generally allow single-player modding, they have been known to take action against content they perceive as harmful to their brand or online ecosystem (e.g., specific GTA RP situations)[6].\n    *   **Monetization Risks:** Most advice on platforms like Reddit suggests that while many YouTubers monetize modded gameplay without issue, it remains a \"gray area\"[1][3]. The primary risk is not necessarily the mod itself, but receiving a copyright claim or strike from the IP holder[3][6].\n*   **Community Consensus:** \n    *   **Avoid Music:** Copyrighted music is a more common trigger for demonetization or strikes than the game footage itself[3].\n    *   **Transformative Content:** Videos that simply showcase a mod without any added value (commentary, editing, storytelling) are often seen as higher risk for copyright issues[4][2].\n    *   **No Guarantees:** Users often caution that just because other YouTubers do it, does not mean it is officially permitted or immune to future enforcement[1][3].\n\n### **Summary of Advice Found on Reddit**\n*   **Risk:** You are operating in a gray area[1]. There is always a risk of copyright claims from the owners of the IP (Marvel/Sony) or the game developer (Rockstar)[6][2].\n*   **Best Practices:** If you choose to proceed, creators often recommend focusing on adding significant transformative value (commentary, editing) and strictly avoiding copyrighted music[3][4][2]. \n*   **Disclaimer:** This information is based on community discussions and general principles of copyright law; it does not constitute legal advice[2]. If you are concerned about your channel, consult the specific EULA/creator guidelines of the game and, if necessary, a legal professional[3][2].\n\nSources:\n[1] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHL9JeSeQZFkb5Nn2PG5pe0r-Me3BgtBUTKKHgkENj3B1AgwBTjbvyADt0UBVYN-AveTmExwRXxYxbEcav0KKP8I7bCMBNTG8FA8CPGBhqel3mGXeP9ZQhmH3GCijxjyxKaPEt59cGZyynTOjCKN0FeRjr_s_bKA-hgTjvwuC0tDgLFtq8e1jg0q6IU45aK-YpZkA5o_yOhxh07K3-pfw==)\n[2] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFNtPQbO5GUfl0TQF_T89mAYyNPzA9F2HF_DE-JmeAmgkZtJ7FpK5RtmIf47OuhqIOT62TDOHUVvnf-DNkJT-kHUUQ6jvvr0U-ez2RAwsyWxPO_lqcEMvk1hxvm226GyjLH0GSa6af9MJijiPGI01g7JsrVOAV4igH7oXlZ6FdKFGVsP_F24yI8o1UzgM22YQU8Gur4LxXj)\n[3] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.co